hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15569","Abu Amir narrated to us: Abd al-Malik, meaning Ibn Hasan al-Harithi, narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Said narrated to us, he said: I heard Umarah ibn Harithah al-Damri narrating, from Amr ibn Yathribi al-Damri, he said: I witnessed the address of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Mina, and among what he addressed with was that he said: It is not lawful for a man from the property of his brother except what his soul is pleased with. He said: When I heard that, I said: O Messenger of Allah, what if I meet the sheep of my cousin and take a sheep from them and slaughter it, is anything upon me in that? He said: If you meet it, a ewe carrying a blade and tinder, do not touch it."
"21397","Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to me, Hatim ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Hasan al-Jari, from Umarah ibn Harithah, from Amr ibn Yathribi, he said, The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, addressed us and said, Nothing of the wealth of his brother is lawful for a man except with the goodwill of his soul, so I said, O Messenger of Allah, what if I meet the sheep of my cousin, shall I take a sheep from them, he said, If you meet it as a ewe carrying a blade and firesticks at Khabt al-Jamish, then do not disturb her, he said, meaning Khabt al-Jamish is a land between Makkah and al-Jar in which there is no human."
"21398","Abu Amir narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn al-Hasan, meaning al-Jari, narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'id narrated to us, he said, I heard Imarah ibn Harithah narrating from Amr ibn Yathribi al-Damri, he said, I witnessed the sermon of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at Mina, and among what he addressed with was that he said, Nothing of the wealth of his brother is lawful for a man except what his soul is willing with, he said, When I heard that I said, O Messenger of Allah, what if I meet the sheep of my cousin and take a sheep from them and slaughter it, is there anything upon me in that, he said, If you meet it as a ewe carrying a blade and firesticks, then do not touch her, this is the end of the Musnad of the Basrans, may Allah be pleased with them."
